    <bpmn:process id="W_W3631" name="W3631. Environmental &amp; Process Instrument Calibration" isExecutable="false">
      <bpmn:documentation>Trigger: Environmental-instrument calibration cycle (W3619); new instrument; threshold excursion
Frequency: Time-based + on excursion
Volume: Temperature/humidity sensors, gas detectors, pressure gauges across DCs/stores/process
Owner: Metrology Manager / Facilities &amp; HSE
Participants: Metrology Manager, Facilities (links to VS-20.3/VS-07.2), HSE (links to VS-24), DC Operations (links to VS-04), Quality (links to VS-31), Calibration Technicians (W3622), Vendor
Source: workflow W3631 — Environmental &amp; Process Instrument Calibration</bpmn:documentation>
      <bpmn:laneSet id="W3631_LaneSet2">
        <bpmn:lane id="W3631_Lane1" name="Metrology Manager">
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3631_Task4</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3631_Task5</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3631_Task6</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3631_Start3</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        <bpmn:flowNodeRef>W3631_End7</bpmn:flowNodeRef>
        </bpmn:lane>
      </bpmn:laneSet>
      <bpmn:startEvent id="W3631_Start3" name="Environmental-instrument calibration cycle (W3619); new instrument; threshold excursion">
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3631_Flow10</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:startEvent>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3631_Task4" name="Metrology Manager/Calibration Technicians calibrate environmental and process…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 1: Metrology Manager/Calibration Technicians calibrate environmental and process instruments: temperature/humidity sensors (paint/chemical storage, DC environmental monitoring links to VS-04), gas detectors (refrigerant/LPG/combustible/toxic), pressure gauges, and process instruments; verify against traceable standards (W3618), adjust, as-left verify, OOT determination (W3634)
Responsible (R): Metrology Manager / Calibration Technicians / Vendor
Accountable (A): Quality Manager
Duration: Per instrument</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3631_Flow10</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3631_Flow11</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3631_Task5" name="Metrology Manager/HSE manage instrument-driven thresholds and alarms: ensure…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 2: Metrology Manager/HSE manage instrument-driven thresholds and alarms: ensure the sensor triggers the correct threshold/alarm (temperature limit for paint storage, gas-leak alarm) and that calibration supports safety/compliance decisions (links to VS-24); manage the calibration interval for safety-critical instruments (shorter, fail-safe)
Responsible (R): Metrology Manager / HSE / Facilities
Accountable (A): Quality Manager / COO
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3631_Flow11</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3631_Flow12</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:userTask id="W3631_Task6" name="Metrology Manager capture records (W3624), respond to OOT and threshold…">
        <bpmn:documentation>Step 3: Metrology Manager capture records (W3624), respond to OOT and threshold excursions (links to W3634/VS-24), and report environmental/process instrument accuracy to governance (W3640); coordinate with facility/DC environmental monitoring (links to VS-04/VS-20.3)
Responsible (R): Metrology Manager / Facilities / HSE
Accountable (A): Quality Manager
Duration: Continuous</bpmn:documentation>
        <bpmn:incoming>W3631_Flow12</bpmn:incoming>
        <bpmn:outgoing>W3631_Flow13</bpmn:outgoing>
      </bpmn:userTask>
      <bpmn:endEvent id="W3631_End7" name="Complete">
        <bpmn:incoming>W3631_Flow13</bpmn:incoming>
      </bpmn:endEvent>
